cy","la":12.153292,"lo":-68.275352,"d":407},{"n":"Caribbean Laundry service and Magero Self Service Laundry","g":"essentials","k":"laundry","la":12.149475,"lo":-68.272648,"d":476},{"n":"Fundashon Mariadal","g":"essentials","k":"hospital","la":12.153841,"lo":-68.274698,"d":494,"w":"https://www.fundashonmariadal.com/"},{"n":"Botica Sabana","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":12.149474,"lo":-68.271439,"d":607,"ph":"+599 717 5638"},{"n":"ATM","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":12.143599,"lo":-68.275834,"d":722},{"n":"BonDiGro","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":12.14488,"lo":-68.271482,"d":827,"w":"https://www.bondigro.com/"},{"n":"Canarbo","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":12.14463,"lo":-68.270744,"d":905,"w":"https://www.canarbo.com"},{"n":"Alfa & Omega Uniforms & Laundry","g":"essentials","k":"laundry","la":12.156716,"lo":-68.271525,"d":954},{"n":"Hamacan Minimarket","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":12.15869,"lo":-68.273768,"d":1028},{"n":"Warehouse Supermarket","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":12.14419,"lo":-68.269507,"d":1039},{"n":"ATM","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":12.152796,"lo":-68.267811,"d":1046},{"n":"MCB","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":12.144186,"lo":-68.269251,"d":1061},{"n":"Fort Orange (Bonaire)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.14883,"lo":-68.27674,"d":133,"ds":"Fort Orange (Dutch: Fort Oranje) is a military fortification in Kralendijk, Bonaire. Originally built in 1639 as a nameless fort by the Dutch West India Company, it is the oldest masonry structure on the island of Bonaire. The fort has never been used for its intended purpose.","wpu":"Fort Orange (Bonaire)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Fort-Oranje.jpg/960px-Fort-Oranje.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St. Bernard Church, Kralendijk","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.1527,"lo":-68.2732,"d":510,"ds":"The St. Bernard Church (Papiamento: Parokia San Bernardo) is a religious building belonging to the Catholic Church and is located in the city of Kralendijk, the capital of the Caribbean island of Bonaire, a territory in the Caribbean Netherlands organised as a special municipality of the Netherlands in the Antilles.","wpu":"St. Bernard Church, Kralendijk","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/BONAIRE-kralendijk-kath-kirche.jpg/960px-BONAIRE-kralendijk-kath-kirche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Bonaire National Marine Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.1717,"lo":-68.2937,"d":3019,"ds":"The Bonaire National Marine Park (BNMP) is one of the oldest marine reserves in the world. It includes the sea around Bonaire and Klein Bonaire from the high water line to a depth of sixty meters (approximately 200 feet). The park was established in 1979 and covers 2700 hectares (6700 acres) and includes a coral reef, seagrass, and mangrove vegetation.","wpu":"Bonaire National Marine Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Kleine_Bonaire-Underwater_life%28js%29.jpg/960px-Kleine_Bonaire-Underwater_life%28js%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Belnem","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.1247,"lo":-68.2882,"d":3065,"ds":"Belnem is a private community on the Dutch Caribbean island of Bonaire. It was named after American singer Harry Belafonte and Aruban businessman Maurice Neme. The area was developed as a luxurious private community starting in 1966, with Belafonte and Neme serving as the first directors of the Bel-Nem Caribbean Development Corporation.","wpu":"Belnem","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/89/Bellafonte_in_Bonaire_%281834766314%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Klein Bonaire","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.158056,"lo":-68.310833,"d":3785,"ds":"Klein Bonaire (Dutch for \"Little Bonaire\") is a small uninhabited islet off the west coast of the Caribbean island of Bonaire, and is part of the Dutch special municipality of Bonaire.","wpu":"Klein Bonaire","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Bonaire_island.png/960px-Bonaire_island.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Bonaire","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.2,"lo":-68.25,"d":6286,"ds":"Bonaire is a Caribbean island in the Leeward Antilles. A special municipality (officially \"public body\") of the Netherlands, its seat is the port of Kralendijk, on the west (leeward) coast of the island. Aruba, Bonaire and Curaçao form the ABC islands, 80 km (50 mi) off the coast of Venezuela.","wpu":"Bonaire","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Flag_of_Bonaire.svg/960px-Flag_of_Bonaire.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Boven Bolivia","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.1819,"lo":-68.2181,"d":7319,"ds":"Boven Bolivia is a hamlet on the island of Bonaire at the head of a lagoon on the island's east coast. Boven Bolivia started as a plantation. Guano was discovered in the late 19th century, however the plantation was later abandoned and only ruins remain.","wpu":"Boven Bolivia","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Collectie_Nationaal_Museum_van_Wereldculturen_TM-20029738_Koe_op_Plantage_Bolivia%2C_met_op_de_achtergrond_een_grote_cactus_en_een_dividiviboom_Bonaire_Boy_Lawson_%28Fotograaf%29.jpg/960px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Lac Bay","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.099722,"lo":-68.233056,"d":7353,"ds":"Lac Bay, also known as Lac Baai, Het Lac, Lac Cai,, or simply Lac, is a shallow bay on the south-eastern coast of the island of Bonaire in the Caribbean Netherlands. It has a fringing reef at its mouth and contains about 100 ha of mangroves as well as a small harbour for fishing vessels. Its seagrass beds are used by sea turtles.","wpu":"Lac Bay","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Magnificent_frigatebird_%28Fregata_magnificens_rothschildi%29_female_with_open_wings.jpg/960px-Magnificent_frigatebird_%28Fregata_magnificens_rothschildi%29_female_with_open_wings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Washikemba–Fontein–Onima Important Bird Area","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.239167,"lo":-68.280556,"d":9922,"ds":"The Washikemba–Fontein–Onima Important Bird Area is a 5,959 ha strip of land along the north-eastern coast of the island of Bonaire in the Caribbean Netherlands. It has been identified as an Important Bird Area by BirdLife International because it supports populations of various threatened or restricted-range bird species.","wpu":"Washikemba–Fontein–Onima Important Bird Area","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Margarops_fuscatus_-Guana_Island%2C_British_Virgin_Islands-8.jpg/960px-Margarops_fuscatus_-Guana_Island%2C_British_Virgin_Islands-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Kralendijk (Dutch pronunciation: [ˈkraːlə(n)dɛik]) is the capital and the main port of the island of Bonaire in the Caribbean Netherlands. The language spoken in the town is Papiamentu, but Dutch and English are widely used. As of 2017, the town had a population of 10,620.","wpu":"Kralendijk","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/BONAIRE-kralendijk-hafen-2.jpg/960px-BONAIRE-kralendijk-hafen-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}